        "prompt": "$\\frac37$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.\\dot42857\\dot1$",
          "worked": "Divide $3$ by $7$. The successive digit calculations are:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}30&=7\\times4+2\\\\20&=7\\times2+6\\\\60&=7\\times8+4\\\\40&=7\\times5+5\\\\50&=7\\times7+1\\\\10&=7\\times1+3\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe remainder returns to $3$, so the cycle repeats.\n\n$$\\frac37=0.428571428571\\ldots=0.\\dot42857\\dot1$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\frac2{11}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.\\dot1\\dot8$",
          "worked": "Divide $2$ by $11$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}20&=11\\times1+9\\\\90&=11\\times8+2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe remainder returns to $2$, so $18$ repeats.\n\n$$\\frac2{11}=0.181818\\ldots=0.\\dot1\\dot8$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac5{12}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.41\\dot6$",
          "worked": "Divide $5$ by $12$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}50&=12\\times4+2\\\\20&=12\\times1+8\\\\80&=12\\times6+8\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe remainder $8$ repeats, so the digit $6$ repeats.\n\n$$\\frac5{12}=0.41666\\ldots=0.41\\dot6$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac6{13}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.\\dot46153\\dot8$",
          "worked": "Divide $6$ by $13$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}60&=13\\times4+8\\\\80&=13\\times6+2\\\\20&=13\\times1+7\\\\70&=13\\times5+5\\\\50&=13\\times3+11\\\\110&=13\\times8+6\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe remainder returns to $6$, so $461538$ repeats.\n\n$$\\frac6{13}=0.461538461538\\ldots=0.\\dot46153\\dot8$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\frac56$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.8\\dot3$",
          "worked": "Divide $5$ by $6$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}50&=6\\times8+2\\\\20&=6\\times3+2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe remainder $2$ repeats, so the digit $3$ repeats.\n\n$$\\frac56=0.83333\\ldots=0.8\\dot3$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
